<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I838abdcb788ed740cd54cf7cc630d6f431918dff" commit="aacb827acdb40f77326eaa652ca23aa4fb534d77" commit_message="Add infra_virtualenv to labtools checkout  BUG=chromium:678360 TEST=None  Change-Id: I838abdcb788ed740cd54cf7cc630d6f431918dff Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/425192 Commit-Ready: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="425192" owner_email="ayatane@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/manifest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/manifest" ref="refs/changes/92/425192/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I026c9a6688e31d95d599008c93092247549930ec" commit="a8c145f9751ea4ff964673d5067ebaa117956433" commit_message="UPSTREAM: groups: Consolidate the setgroups permission checks  Today there are 3 instances of setgroups and due to an oversight their permission checking has diverged.  Add a common function so that they may all share the same permission checking code.  This corrects the current oversight in the current permission checks and adds a helper to avoid this in the future.  A user namespace security fix will update this new helper, shortly.  Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org Signed-off-by: &quot;Eric W. Biederman&quot; &lt;ebiederm@xmission.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 7ff4d90b4c24a03666f296c3d4878cd39001e81e) Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I026c9a6688e31d95d599008c93092247549930ec Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424911 Commit-Ready: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="424911" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/11/424911/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I69deefd4c2dfa1e5dd92f8f49c0685fd7408868d" commit="ccf4e4fb5b2cd43cc52ec7811f2df74afb7ee7ea" commit_message="BACKPORT: userns: Don't allow setgroups until a gid mapping has been setablished  setgroups is unique in not needing a valid mapping before it can be called, in the case of setgroups(0, NULL) which drops all supplemental groups.  The design of the user namespace assumes that CAP_SETGID can not actually be used until a gid mapping is established.  Therefore add a helper function to see if the user namespace gid mapping has been established and call that function in the setgroups permission check.  This is part of the fix for CVE-2014-8989, being able to drop groups without privilege using user namespaces.  dgreid - context conflicts only  Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org Reviewed-by: Andy Lutomirski &lt;luto@amacapital.net&gt; Signed-off-by: &quot;Eric W. Biederman&quot; &lt;ebiederm@xmission.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 273d2c67c3e179adb1e74f403d1e9a06e3f841b5)  Change-Id: I69deefd4c2dfa1e5dd92f8f49c0685fd7408868d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/425152 Commit-Ready: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="425152" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/52/425152/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ieac44ded347160d4e44033e6383c013c9d25d4d6" commit="85028c35b650d34728e12b046582441734223fed" commit_message="UPSTREAM: userns: Rename id_map_mutex to userns_state_mutex  Generalize id_map_mutex so it can be used for more state of a user namespace.  Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org Reviewed-by: Andy Lutomirski &lt;luto@amacapital.net&gt; Signed-off-by: &quot;Eric W. Biederman&quot; &lt;ebiederm@xmission.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit f0d62aec931e4ae3333c797d346dc4f188f454ba) Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: Ieac44ded347160d4e44033e6383c013c9d25d4d6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/425153 Commit-Ready: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="425153" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/53/425153/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I4e224e91d4cf8ae8d64a67de45dd4c91f16a5e53" commit="f01b02ff82bf30ec53d67accba3acf8cd027ffed" commit_message="BACKPORT: userns: Add a knob to disable setgroups on a per user namespace basis  - Expose the knob to user space through a proc file /proc/&lt;pid&gt;/setgroups    A value of &quot;deny&quot; means the setgroups system call is disabled in the   current processes user namespace and can not be enabled in the   future in this user namespace.    A value of &quot;allow&quot; means the segtoups system call is enabled.  - Descendant user namespaces inherit the value of setgroups from   their parents.  - A proc file is used (instead of a sysctl) as sysctls currently do   not allow checking the permissions at open time.  - Writing to the proc file is restricted to before the gid_map   for the user namespace is set.    This ensures that disabling setgroups at a user namespace   level will never remove the ability to call setgroups   from a process that already has that ability.    A process may opt in to the setgroups disable for itself by   creating, entering and configuring a user namespace or by calling   setns on an existing user namespace with setgroups disabled.   Processes without privileges already can not call setgroups so this   is a noop.  Prodcess with privilege become processes without   privilege when entering a user namespace and as with any other path   to dropping privilege they would not have the ability to call   setgroups.  So this remains within the bounds of what is possible   without a knob to disable setgroups permanently in a user namespace.  dgreid - context conflicts only  Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org Signed-off-by: &quot;Eric W. Biederman&quot; &lt;ebiederm@xmission.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 9cc46516ddf497ea16e8d7cb986ae03a0f6b92f8) Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I4e224e91d4cf8ae8d64a67de45dd4c91f16a5e53 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/425154 Commit-Ready: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="425154" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/425154/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iccd9ca8395d7c6067cb0abd4860f7f1930665e4f" commit="8cccc90523ec6d5f04db098a7377c064f4548998" commit_message="linux-firmware: USE flag support for audio on KBL  Include adsp_kbl USE flag for adding static firmware binary to support audio.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57131 TEST=emerge-{BOARD} linux-firmware installs the dsp_fw_kbl.bin in the right place(/lib/firmware/intel)  Change-Id: Iccd9ca8395d7c6067cb0abd4860f7f1930665e4f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402649 Commit-Ready: Chintan M Patel &lt;chintan.m.patel@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Ca