d another thread in gk20a_set_error_notifier() is still using the error notifier.  Fix this by introducing mutex error_notifier_mutex for error notifier accesses.  In gk20a_init_error_notifier(), set the pointer ch-&gt;error_notifier_ref inside the mutex and only after notifier is completely initialized.  This patch fixes a security vulnerability reported here: https://code.google.com/p/android/issues/detail?id=224268  Change-Id: I4d2a787d5e4fad2c05c014682597010fc95566f5 Signed-off-by: Deepak Nibade &lt;dnibade@nvidia.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424655 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="424655" owner_email="markz@gpartner-nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/55/424655/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I546f9f099f45654091e9505d517cc3908bff3ae6" commit="d2794b37bfb6f463cfa8fa591719046990fe8f3b" commit_message="Updated the function to get  image_name.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I546f9f099f45654091e9505d517cc3908bff3ae6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424795 Commit-Ready: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aashutosh Kalyankar &lt;aashutoshk@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aashutosh Kalyankar &lt;aashutoshk@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="424795" owner_email="aashutoshk@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/95/424795/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id976fc47955b33ca83bb2182b197d9f2781c341b" commit="bb2a0df461c0d6be2690e1ec509d7d31d8ce4a08" commit_message="core: Fix bug will cause tasks sleep forever by mutex_unlock in task.c.  If there's a task switching occurred between loading waiter and unlocking the lock, the task with higher priority won't wake up since the local variable, waiter, doesn't contain its ID bit before task switching. In this situation, the higher priority task only can be awakened when the other tasks execute mutex_unlock() again.  But consider the following conditions: (For example, the driver of charger bd9995x.) 1. There are more than one mutex for the usage path of i2c port. 2. There are more than one task access this usage path of i2c port and    one of these tasks, task A, met the situation above. 3. The other tasks have no chance to execute mutex_unlock() of i2c since    the task A still occupied the mutex of charger.  All the tasks used the same i2c port or the other hardware will sleep forever. This CL makes loading waiter and unlocking the lock as atomic to solve this issue.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:60617 TEST=make BOARD=snappy; make BOARD=oak; Executed charger factory test on 4 units of snappy for 3 days and no symptom occurred.  Change-Id: Id976fc47955b33ca83bb2182b197d9f2781c341b Signed-off-by: Mulin Chao &lt;mlchao@nuvoton.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423285 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423285" owner_email="mlchao@nuvoton.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/85/423285/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibbfc2bcdf1f43b40d51e62e75b93a39f97d59448" commit="0e85451c9a344740aeaba21d50ca890057dfdb65" commit_message="Added timeout to adb commands  Adb commands from the AdbHost will now timeout just like fastboot commands.  BUG=b:33562943 TEST=Ran single test.  Change-Id: Ibbfc2bcdf1f43b40d51e62e75b93a39f97d59448 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423256 Commit-Ready: Kris Rambish &lt;krisr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Benjamin Peake &lt;bpeake@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kris Rambish &lt;krisr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kris Rambish &lt;krisr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="423256" owner_email="bpeake@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/56/423256/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If28ae2727181845946c9f36a34716779fb4343a6" commit="8a7660ca17111a2163695d773edb92188400ea8d" commit_message="Add pylint to pip_packages  BUG=chromium:571100 TEST=None  Change-Id: If28ae2727181845946c9f36a34716779fb4343a6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/424909 Commit-Ready: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="424909" owner_email="ayatane@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/infra_virtualenv" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/infra_virtualenv" ref="refs/changes/09/424909/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If4bd8e4f132ea80d0aadaa221b5e81f8d136097a" commit="a2518304d7b65d5cab46c868bd90dd1d5c081234" commit_message="chipset-kbl: add the LPE related USE flags  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57131 TEST=emerge-{BOARD} linux-firmware installs the dsp_fw_kbl.bin in the right place(/lib/firmware/intel)  Change-Id: If4bd8e4f132ea80d0aadaa221b5e81f8d136097a Signed-off-by: Chintan Patel &lt;chintan.m.patel@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/403108 Commit-Ready: Chintan M Patel &lt;chintan.m.pa